  "prefLabel": "Lot 7102.19 Role-based access control",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lot 7102.19 “Role-based access control” means a principle by which developers create systems that limit access or restrict operations according to a user’s constructed role within a system. This system is used by businesses and organizations to ensure that unauthorized users do not gain access to privileged information within an IT architecture. Role-based access control is also known as role-based security.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Lot 7100) #13068, eff 6-27-20; ss by #13913, eff 3-22-24 (formerly Lot 7102.16)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lot7100.html"
